fix(hwmon): an unsampled TAS2764 amplifier reads 0 C, not a failure

The TAS2764 speaker amplifier samples its die temperature only while it
is powered for audio. A power cycle, as on every resume from suspend,
clears the register, and the driver then answers ENODATA until audio
plays. The daemon took that as a failed read: the channel went to
failsafe with an error on every resume, and at a start before any audio
the channel was dropped for the whole session. A Mac carries six of
these amplifiers.

ENODATA from a tas2764 device is now read as 0.0 C with one info line,
the treatment the daemon already gives a powered-down ThinkPad GPU and
a sleeping drive, and the channel is kept at detection. Every other
device and every other error is unchanged.

Measured on a J316c MacBook Pro (M1 Max), kernel 7.1.13: six
"Significant issue retrieving status for hwmon device: tas2764" after a
resume at 22:37, recovered at 23:11 once audio played.

